#uuid "e257c7be-72fa-5044-afd5-3c231c4d2101" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402330} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d961e8a-0a6f-54c1-8cde-ab0903529501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402336} {:answer/id #uuid "c6754a7b-081e-5d31-992c-2069f9dc057c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "discontinuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402337}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402336} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b9f9176-6990-5c20-b84c-e134dd361960" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9937b4b8-0233-5d12-b8c0-111d5bfd92fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-343445" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-4, & x\\in [-\\pi ,0] \\\\ 2, & x\\in (0,\\pi )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{\\pi (2n-1)}sin\\,((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nAt $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-1+\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-n\\pi )=(-1)^{n}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-4.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-1+\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\ -4 & =-1+\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot (-1)^{n} \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bc78a68d-4643-5a86-980c-c8ebf837e55e"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506657 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06015b37-c1da-5c8e-878c-60947fbc840c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315148} {:answer/id #uuid "24ea2114-3bd1-52c4-bf57-325363fd5bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315325} {:answer/id #uuid "a81de909-9548-5ec4-8d3c-1983bf705587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316061}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315325} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c781efb-4362-5ebb-94b7-8bf35aea1ea4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316767} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ed29729-d42b-5f9d-81b4-fac91b47193e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "discontinuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315651} {:answer/id #uuid "70cfcbc1-b8b9-5044-9c8f-66a69b6cebb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315754}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315754} :answer-field/id #uuid "62a481c8-ee27-5287-8fe1-cf0b98ba368c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/typ